read("all") retries a read that a signal interrupted instead of treating it
as end of file, whether or not data arrived before the interruption.

libubox installs its SIGCHLD handler without SA_RESTART, so in a uloop based
host (rpcd, uhttpd, ...) any child exiting while the VM is blocked in a read
interrupts that read with EINTR.

-- Testcase --
{%
	import * as uloop from 'uloop';
	import { popen, error } from 'fs';

	uloop.init();

	// An unrelated child that exits while we are blocked reading
	let other = popen('sleep 1', 'r');

	let proc = popen('sleep 2; echo payload', 'r');

	let data = proc.read('all');

	printf('data: %J\nerror: %J\nexit: %d\n', data, error(), proc.close());

	other.close();
	uloop.done();
%}
-- End --

-- Expect stdout --
data: "payload\n"
error: null
exit: 0
-- End --
